  {
    "episode_id": 78079,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78079.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, you got to get elected every six years or two years. That's been the case with me. So you've got to satisfy the electorate. First of all, I love my work. I think maybe one of the things that helped because I'm 87 years old that at 65, I started running. Now I don't like to use the word run. I kind of shuffle along but i try to stay physically active and then i enjoy my constituent you know three million constituents of which obviously i don't get the votes of all of them but i try to stay in touch with them you have to know what They think if you're going to represent the people. And I like to also promote the concept of representative government. If you're going to have it, you got to have dialogue between our constituents and those of us elected. So that's why every year for 40 years, I go to every county of the 99 counties every year for having dialogue with my constituents so that no part of the state can say I forgot about them and that's what you have to do. So I've been in 22 counties so far this year.",
