    "turn_text": "that'll be 42 years in the United States, seven, six years in the US House. and 16 years in the Iowa House of Representatives. So Senator, I'm curious, should there be term limits on senators? I haven't voted on it recently, but the only time it's come up, I voted for term limits of two. You also got to think in terms of, there really can be term limits if the people want them. by every six years, they got a chance to vote us out of office. So there's term limits that way. And I think it's probably been 15 or 20 years since it's been an Asian Congress. And you have to amend the Constitution to accomplish it. So it would take a two thirds vote in the United States Senate. And I think when it was up in the United States Senate, it probably got in the mid 50s. So it came up short of the two thirds vote, but I voted for two or three times.",
