  {
    "episode_id": 78079,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78079.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "Well, you have to accept it or you shouldn't be in it. And what you really criticism is perfectly legitimate. But a lot of criticism is unfair criticism. And that's what I resent. And I particularly resent it when people get the wrong view from the media and they don't, they don't think it through and they think that what they read in the media is really your motivation. I'll give you an example of the bill that passed two weeks or a week ago, this last image bill. every Republican voted against it. We did support one-third of it, about $600 billion, because it was directly related to the pandemic. But a lot of things that were in the other two-thirds that were unrelated to the pandemic was nothing but a Democrat wish-less. So the Des Moines Register Rights and article saying all the things we voted again, but they didn't give people any Idea what we were really for and that doesn't take into consideration the fact that four or five previous bills have passed last year that passed with 90 over 90 votes in the United States Senate, and they were all bipartisan. But now the Democrats wanted to go partisan. So then we have to write an op-ed piece to the Des Moines Register, Senator Ernst, and I do, explaining what we were for. So we get criticized for what the editorial says, but they don't tell the complete story. So it's that sort of criticism that irritates you. I don't expect everybody to agree with me.",
