  {
    "episode_id": 78079,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78079.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "First of all, whatever profession you're in, including your profession, if you're a Christian, you ought to live that every day. It's kind of like, preach Christ, but use words only when necessary. And it's the same thing you hear from the pulpit and archer. And so I think that it is a much different between what you do daily and I do daily. The only thing is that when you're a senator and there's a hundred of us, the focus is on it. On us more than it's on you so i think you have to be a little more careful or it's easy to be called a hypocrite and i don't and sometimes maybe i'm legitimately called a hypocrite because you know there's nothing perfect about us like there was jesus christ So I always try to tell people to read 1 Timothy 2 1 and 2 and pray for those of us in government. I try to set an example where I can, when I have disagreements with people, I try not to be disagreeable. And I think just live in day to day to be a living example of what Christ stood for is the best way to be a witness for you.",
