  {
    "episode_id": 78079,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78079.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "Well, Senator, I am a parent of three daughters. I have a 19-year-old, a 17-year-old, and a 14-year-old. And we talk about politics, but they constantly bring up just the divisiveness. And there's so many negatives from their perspective to engaging in politics. And so why should young people consider maybe even serving in government when they see so much criticism, so many challenges that come with it? How would you encourage younger people to engage or maybe even serve?",
