  {
    "episode_id": 78079,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78079.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "First of all, there is too much to visit us, but not as much as they think because journalism is all about reporting dissension and fighting and disagreement. It's almost like people think Republicans don't talk to Democrats. That's not right. If you want to know about Chuck Grassley, go to the Georgetown University website and click on Lugar Institute. And they do surveys every year of 100 senators and rate them from the most bipartisan to the least bipartisan. And I always come in the top 10. So I really don't have any problems. But socially and even business-wise, you can have very friendly discussions with Democrats as a Republican. And sometimes I get along with some democrats better and I get along with some republicans. So you get a distorted picture of it. It's not as bad as they think, but it still is not good. So I'm not detracting from what your daughters are telling you. But on the other hand, why do it? Because in America, whether you served here or you just want to be a voter or you just want to participate in the political party or whether you want to, you know, run for office, whatever you want to do. In America, you have an opportunity to help govern or be governed. And I would hope your daughters would choose being a part of the process in governing. If you expect the Congress, the United States to be representative of our constituents, understand our society as a whole, not just the Congress, but society as a whole is less civil than they were 15 years ago. So some of that's reflected in the Congress of the United States if we're going to be a representative body. And if you want to do away with it and have a different environment, do away with social media, do away with all the talk show radio, do away with all the cable television, go back to when ABC, CBS, NBC ran the news, and then you didn't have so much of that. On the other hand, We have more democracy now than we ever had before, because there isn't a thing your daughters can't say through social media and get it out there about government and about politics. So I think our even though we have the bad. aspect of being divided. We also have easier participation at the grassroots of America in the governmental process and the discussion of policy issues.",
