    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/8/78079.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "That is such a good perspective. I love help govern or be governed and just championing the idea of representative government, which is really so essential. And we mentioned Reagan earlier, and I remember in 84, he won 49 states in re-election. Can you see that happening again in a presidential candidate? Can you see? No. No. I have shared that because I work a lot with Generation Z2 and I've shared that with people and it's mind-blowing to them that one candidate could garner that much approval. And so we've talked a little bit just about the challenge of really knowing what's true, but how does just the average everyday American island know what's true and wade through all of that to know what's really going on? And how do they sort through that?",
